      "text": "CONTEXT:\n  - Counter-Reformation (Council of Trent 1545-1563):\n    Church instructs art to be emotionally compelling,\n    accessible, doctrinally unambiguous\n  - Protestant Reformation in the North:\n    Iconoclasm in Netherlands, Germany -- dramatic reduction\n    in church commissions; rise of secular genres\n  - Absolute monarchy (France, Spain): art as state apparatus\n  - Scientific Revolution: observation, empiricism in art mirrors\n    empirical methods in science (contemporary with Galileo, Bacon)"
